The black hole should be a physical-looking object; the accretion disk should be the spectacle; the particles should add detail rather than define the entire image.
Your screenshot already has a useful particle foundation. Keep it, but stop asking the particle system to create the black hole, its lighting, and the gravitational lensing all by itself.
The implementation below assumes React Three Fiber, Three.js, and TypeScript. It uses GPU-friendly particles, shader-based disk rendering, and a post-processing pass for lensing.

