I'd implement the visual changes in this order:
A clearly defined black silhouette.
A continuous luminous disk behind and in front of it.
Differential orbital motion.
Screen-space gravitational-lensing approximation.
Bloom, exposure, and subtle turbulence.
Don't start by increasing your particle count. Start by improving the composition and the light.
2. Install the rendering dependencies
If you already have an R3F project, keep your existing dependencies and add the post-processing packages:
npm install three @react-three/fiber @react-three/postprocessing postprocessing
Use compatible versions of Three.js, R3F, and React Postprocessing rather than upgrading the entire project blindly. React Postprocessing supports custom GLSL effects and composes them into an effect pipeline.
