+1
How to tune it
Lensing strength

Subtle → dramatic
Start at 0.002. Raise it gradually and watch for excessive stretching.
Influence radius
Start at 0.23 in aspect-corrected screen coordinates. A larger value affects more of the image.
Important limitation
This effect warps the entire rendered image, including foreground particles and the black-hole silhouette. It is a cinematic distortion, not a physical ray tracer. Use it as a prototype; for convincing lensing, the next step is to render the disk and background into separate layers or trace rays through a black-hole spacetime.
For a proper relativistic renderer, you would trace camera rays backward through the gravitational field, integrate their paths, and sample the disk or background where the rays terminate. A Schwarzschild model is a reasonable starting point for a non-rotating black hole; a Kerr model is needed to account for spin.
6. Get the cinematic lighting right
Bloom is what lets bright pixels spread light into neighboring pixels, creating the luminous halo. It works best when your disk has genuine bright regions, rather than when everything is equally bright. React Postprocessing provides a Bloom effect that can be combined with other effects in the composer.
